[Music]  here we go again  sony have finally revealed the free  games for us playstation plus  subscribers for the month  of march 2021 like always we can  download these games from the first  tuesday of the month which is march the  2nd  you ready let's do this i can't believe  i'm saying this but on ps4 in march we  can get our hands on one of last year's  most anticipated games  final fantasy 7 remake you've likely  heard about the jrpg from back in 1997  and maybe you've played it too  the remake retells a portion of that  story but doubles down on the character  development and story  the rpg elements remain key but without  a doubt  this is as much an action game as it is  an rpg  playing as cloud strife we are recruited  into avalanche a group  facing off against the mega corporations  in the world you'll be blowing up a  reactor or two and wielding a sword  which is feasibly impossible to pick up  if you're worried about turn-based  combat  don't be everything has been updated to  allow for real-time action  as our abilities build up before we can  harness them  adding a different type of tactical play  than simply spamming a button repeatedly  we aren't stuck to one character either  the party members can be switched to on  the fly  if you're not too great with barrett you  know the guy with a gun for an arm  let the ai take over that person which  allows you to concentrate on the  characters you prefer  once you've been playing a few hours  though you'll be switching between  everyone instinctively  definitely give this a go even if final  fantasy games haven't been your jam in  the past  i promise it's worth it game number two  is here on the ps5  this is marquette a first person puzzle  adventure  how the heck can i explain this well one  example shows how the world is within a  world  here's a large block which requires  moving and to do that the player uses  a miniature model to move it and voila  in the real world the block has  moved to this goes further with a world  inside a world inside a world it's like  inception after learning how things work  in this environment you'll be using  different versions of each world to  impact your progress  like using a key from the upper world to  bridge across a gap  in the current world it's tough to  explain in 60 seconds but i think you  get the idea  marquette looks to test your logic  thoroughly  back over to the ps4 now and remnant  from the ashes  another role-playing action game but  this one is much more shooter-based  the game is best described as a  soulsborne game  but with guns remnant is said to be a  difficult game  in other words remnant will make you  fail and thus learn from your mistakes  and then adapt in your next encounter  difficulty should be expected  so if you're here for games to chill out  with maybe avoid this one  remnant utilizes randomly generated maps  which makes every encounter feel  familiar yet  unique and when coupled up with co-op  play this game is at its best  so to surmise if you're looking for dark  souls with guns  remnant is the game for you game number  four now and  holy heck psvr is getting some love this  is farpoint  back in 2017 this was revolutionary  stuff but four years later  it certainly feels old we joined the  space adventure on a hostile alien  planet and we use an assortment of  weapons and upgrades  to fight off the locals including a  spider big enough to give you  arachnophobia in addition to that single  player stuff there is a co-op mode which  adds much more replayability and teaming  up with a friend to strategize is great  fun  i guess all we need now is a friend rip  the dream  keep in mind farpoint is a 2017 game and  i think you'll enjoy this  but wait there's more we have a sneak  peek at april's ps plus with the  confirmation that ps5 owners will  receive oddworld  soulstorm on the day it releases that's  april the 6th  i'll tell you more about that nearer the  time just thought i'd give you a heads  up  and speaking of the ps5 remember last  month's ps5 game is here for a second  month destruction all stars a take on  destruction derby  but with a twist okie dokie doodoo  that's the games for the month  like usual sound off in the comments and  please rate the month i'm going to give  this  8.7 out of 10. i don't know where that  number came from what do you say  i'm adam from playstation grenade it's  been a pleasure i'll see you next time

